{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "clm_templates",
  "description": "Expression-template library for the CTSM/CLM land-surface soil and bare-ground components (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the pointwise closure laws of ctsm5.4.063 (cesm3.0-alphabranch checkout) exercised by the bare-ground fluxes (stage2/clm_bareground.esm), the soil temperature (stage2/clm_soiltemp.esm) and the soil fluxes (stage2/clm_soilfluxes.esm) components: the QSat saturation vapor pressure/specific humidity laws (qsat_esat/qsat_qs; the dT derivatives qsat_esat_dT/qsat_qsdT follow with the canopy component), the Monin-Obukhov surface-layer laws of the bare-ground fluxes (the Paulson (1970) stability functions - the scalar one is the CMEPS psixhu_unstable law of flux_atmocn_Large.F90:164, inlined here byte-identical from stage2 cmeps_templates.esm until the cmeps bulk-flux component is ported, at which point this library will import it by reference (esm-spec 9.7.3); the momentum one is authored fresh because its constant is SHR_CONST_PI*0.5 while the cmeps psimhu_unstable hard-codes 1.571, with the chik = sqrt(sqrt(1-16*zeta)) intermediate factored as stability_chik), the MoninObukIni initialization laws (wind speed, bulk Richardson number, initial zeta through the shared clamp_zeta), the four-branch friction-velocity profile laws (momentum and scalar, taking the stability parameter zeta as a parameter and sharing the stable branches as stable_profile_integral), the Meier2022 roughness laws (z0hg and the snowmelt-dependent z0mg), the Magnus dewpoint law, the virtual potential temperature scale/difference law (virtual_potential_scale, shared by dthv and thvstar), the BareGroundFluxes flux laws (sensible_heat_flux, evaporation_flux, wind_stress_component, ref2m_profile), the soil/snow thermal laws (snow bulk density, Sturm1997 snow thermal conductivity, snow heat capacity, Johansen (1975) soil thermal conductivity, de Vries (1963) soil heat capacity, harmonic-mean interface conductivity) and the SoilFluxes laws (ground_temperature_blend, stefan_boltzmann_emission, flux_temperature_correction, stefan_boltzmann_emission_dT). Transcribed exactly from the Fortran; every template carries its source file:line in its description and returns one scalar (the CLM laws are all pointwise, so a template per output is sufficient). The remaining shared laws (canopy interception/storage/excess, ZengWang2007 vegetation roughness, emissivities, latent heat of vaporization, Jordan1991 snow conductivity, soil/snow albedo and hydraulics, etc.) will be added here as their stage-2 components (clm_canopy.esm, clm_surfalbedo.esm, clm_atm_forcing.esm) are implemented. Reference: stage1/cesm/components/clm/src/biogeophys/.",
  "tags": [
   "land_surface",
   "clm",
   "soil",
   "bare-ground",
   "expression-templates",
   "cesm"
  ],
  "created": "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z",
  "authors": [
   "EqESM project contributors"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Lawrence, D. M., Fisher, R. A., Koven, C. D., Oleson, K. W., Swenson, S. C., Bonan, G., et al. (2019). The Community Land Model Version 5: Description of New Features, Benchmarking, and Impact of Forcing Uncertainty. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(12), 4245-4287.",
    "doi": "10.1029/2018MS001583"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Meier, R., Davin, E. L., Bonan, G. B., Lawrence, D. M., Hu, X., Duveiller, G., Prigent, C., and Seneviratne, S. I. (2022). Impacts of a revised surface roughness parameterization in the Community Land Model 5.1. Geoscientific Model Development, 15(6), 2365-2393.",
    "doi": "10.5194/gmd-15-2365-2022"
   },
   {
    "citation": "CTSM (Community Terrestrial Systems Model), ESCOMP/CTSM, ctsm5.4.063 (cesm3.0-alphabranch): the CLM land-surface source - QSatMod.F90, FrictionVelocityMod.F90, BareGroundFluxesMod.F90, SoilFluxesMod.F90, SoilTemperatureMod.F90, clm_varcon.F90 (constants) - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
    "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CTSM"
   },
   {
    "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
    "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
   }
  ],
  "license": "MIT"
 },
 "expression_templates": {
  "poly8": {
   "description": "Ninth-order power-sum polynomial c0 + c1*x + ... + c8*x^8, the mathematical form of the Flatau et al. (1992) saturation-vapor-pressure fits used by QSat (QSatMod.F90:18-56). Written as a power sum rather than the Fortran's nested Horner form (QSatMod.F90:93-97) for readability; the two agree to round-off.",
   "params": [
    "c0",
    "c1",
    "c2",
    "c3",
    "c4",
    "c5",
    "c6",
    "c7",
    "c8",
    "x"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "c0",
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c1",
       "x"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c2",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "x",
         2
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c3",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "x",
         3
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c4",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "x",
         4
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c5",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "x",
         5
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c6",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "x",
         6
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c7",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "x",
         7
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "c8",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "x",
         8
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "qsat_esat": {
   "description": "Saturation vapor pressure es(T) [Pa]: QSatMod.F90:90-100. td = min(100, max(-75, T - TKFRZ)); the water polynomial (coefficients a0..a8, QSatMod.F90:18-26) for td >= 0, the ice polynomial (c0..c8, QSatMod.F90:38-46) otherwise, scaled by 100 to Pa.",
   "params": [
    "T",
    "TKFRZ"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     100.0,
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">=",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "min",
          "args": [
           100.0,
           {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
             -75.0,
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "T",
               "TKFRZ"
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         0.0
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "poly8",
        "bindings": {
         "c0": 6.11213476,
         "c1": 0.444007856,
         "c2": 0.0143064234,
         "c3": 0.000264461437,
         "c4": 3.05903558e-06,
         "c5": 1.96237241e-08,
         "c6": 8.92344772e-11,
         "c7": -3.7320841e-13,
         "c8": 2.09339997e-16,
         "x": {
          "op": "min",
          "args": [
           100.0,
           {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
             -75.0,
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "T",
               "TKFRZ"
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       },
       {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "poly8",
        "bindings": {
         "c0": 6.11123516,
         "c1": 0.503109514,
         "c2": 0.0188369801,
         "c3": 0.000420547422,
         "c4": 6.14396778e-06,
         "c5": 6.02780717e-08,
         "c6": 3.87940929e-10,
         "c7": 1.49436277e-12,
         "c8": 2.62655803e-15,
         "x": {
          "op": "min",
          "args": [
           100.0,
           {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
             -75.0,
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "T",
               "TKFRZ"
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "qsat_qs": {
   "description": "Saturation specific humidity qs(T,p) [kg/kg]: QSatMod.F90:101-103. vp = 1/(p - 0.378*es) [1/Pa]; qs = es * 0.622 * vp, with 0.622 and 0.378 the Rd/Rv molecular-weight ratios written bare in the Fortran. Shares qsat_esat by reference.",
   "params": [
    "T",
    "p",
    "TKFRZ"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "qsat_esat",
      "bindings": {
       "T": "T",
       "TKFRZ": "TKFRZ"
      }
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.622,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       1.0,
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "p",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 0.378,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "qsat_esat",
            "bindings": {
             "T": "T",
             "TKFRZ": "TKFRZ"
            }
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "soil_saturation_water_content": {
   "description": "Soil water saturation satw = min(1, (h2osoi_liq/denh2o + h2osoi_ice/denice + excess_ice/denice)/(dz*watsat)) [1]: SoilTemperatureMod.F90:712-713. excess_ice is the excess-ice water equivalent (use_excess_ice = .true. in the run; 0 for all dumped columns).",
   "params": [
    "h2osoi_liq",
    "h2osoi_ice",
    "excess_ice",
    "dz",
    "watsat",
    "denh2o",
    "denice"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "min",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 1.0,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "h2osoi_liq",
           "denh2o"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "h2osoi_ice",
           "denice"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "excess_ice",
           "denice"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "dz",
         "watsat"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "kersten_number": {
   "description": "Kersten number dke [1] of the Johansen (1975) soil thermal conductivity: SoilTemperatureMod.F90:715-719. dke = satw for frozen soil (t_soisno < tfrz), dke = max(0, log10(satw) + 1) for unfrozen soil.",
   "params": [
    "satw",
    "t_soisno",
    "tfrz"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": ">=",
      "args": [
       "t_soisno",
       "tfrz"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "max",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "log10",
          "args": [
           "satw"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     "satw"
    ]
   }
  },
  "soil_liquid_fraction": {
   "description": "Liquid fraction of soil water fl = (h2osoi_liq/(denh2o*dz))/(h2osoi_liq/(denh2o*dz) + h2osoi_ice/(denice*dz) + excess_ice/(denice*dz)) [1]: SoilTemperatureMod.F90:721-723.",
   "params": [
    "h2osoi_liq",
    "h2osoi_ice",
    "excess_ice",
    "dz",
    "denh2o",
    "denice"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "h2osoi_liq",
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "denh2o",
         "dz"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         "h2osoi_liq",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "denh2o",
           "dz"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         "h2osoi_ice",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "denice",
           "dz"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         "excess_ice",
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "denice",
           "dz"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "soil_saturated_thermal_cond": {
   "description": "Saturated soil thermal conductivity dksat = tkmg*tkwat^(fl*watsat)*tkice^((1-fl)*watsat) [W/m/K] of the Johansen (1975) law: SoilTemperatureMod.F90:724. tkmg is the saturated conductivity of the mineral matrix (tkmg = tkm^(1-watsat) from the soil-texture initialization, SoilStateInitTimeConstMod.F90:581), so the exponent (1-watsat) is folded in; fl is the liquid fraction of soil water.",
   "params": [
    "tkmg",
    "fl",
    "watsat",
    "tkwat",
    "tkice"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     "tkmg",
     {
      "op": "^",
      "args": [
       "tkwat",
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "fl",
         "watsat"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "^",
      "args": [
       "tkice",
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.0,
            "units": "1"
           },
           "fl"
          ]
         },
         "watsat"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "soil_thermal_cond": {
   "description": "Soil thermal conductivity thk [W/m/K] of the Johansen (1975) law as implemented in SoilTemperatureMod.F90:712-727, in the named-intermediate form: thk = dke*dksat + (1-dke)*tkdry when satw > 1e-7 (the Fortran threshold is the .1e-6_r8 literal = 1e-7), thk = tkdry otherwise, with the saturation water content satw, the Kersten number dke and the saturated conductivity dksat as NAMED intermediate parameters, each defined once by the caller from soil_saturation_water_content, kersten_number and soil_saturated_thermal_cond (the ESM template format admits params + body only, so naming the intermediates once requires the caller to compute them as observeds: clm_soiltemp.esm declares satw/dke/fl/dksat exactly that way; the bedrock override thk_bedrock at :727 is applied by the caller's layer mask).",
   "params": [
    "satw",
    "dke",
    "dksat",
    "tkdry"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": ">",
      "args": [
       "satw",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 1e-07,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "dke",
         "dksat"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.0,
            "units": "1"
           },
           "dke"
          ]
         },
         "tkdry"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     "tkdry"
    ]
   }
  },
  "soil_heat_capacity": {
   "description": "Soil heat capacity cv = csol*(1-watsat)*dz + h2osoi_ice*cpice + h2osoi_liq*cpliq + excess_ice*cpice [J/m2/K] (de Vries, 1963), per unit ground area: SoilTemperatureMod.F90:852-854. csol is the mineral+organic matrix volumetric heat capacity, watsat the porosity; the dump pins only the product csol*(1-watsat).",
   "params": [
    "csol",
    "watsat",
    "dz",
    "h2osoi_ice",
    "h2osoi_liq",
    "excess_ice",
    "cpice",
    "cpliq"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "csol",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         "watsat"
        ]
       },
       "dz"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "h2osoi_ice",
       "cpice"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "h2osoi_liq",
       "cpliq"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "excess_ice",
       "cpice"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "clm_interface_conductivity": {
   "description": "Harmonic-mean thermal conductivity tk [W/m/K] at the interface between two adjacent layers, from the assumption that the flux across the interface equals the flux from each node to the interface: tk = thk1*thk2*(z2-z1)/(thk1*(z2-zi) + thk2*(zi-z1)) with thk1/thk2 the layer conductivities, z1/z2 the layer-center depths and zi the interface depth between them (SoilTemperatureMod.F90:825-826). The bottom of the column carries no interface (tk = 0 at :828; handled by the caller).",
   "params": [
    "thk1",
    "thk2",
    "z1",
    "z2",
    "zi"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "thk1",
       "thk2",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "z2",
         "z1"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "thk1",
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "z2",
           "zi"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "thk2",
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "zi",
           "z1"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "snow_bulk_density": {
   "description": "Snow bulk density bw = (h2osoi_ice + h2osoi_liq)/(frac_sno_fluxes*dz) [kg/m3]: SoilTemperatureMod.F90:744. frac_sno_fluxes is the snow-covered fraction used for heat-flux calculations (0..1); the stage-1 W3 dump exercises frac_sno_fluxes = 1 exactly.",
   "params": [
    "h2osoi_ice",
    "h2osoi_liq",
    "frac_sno_fluxes",
    "dz"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       "h2osoi_ice",
       "h2osoi_liq"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "frac_sno_fluxes",
       "dz"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "snow_thermal_cond_sturm1997": {
   "description": "Snow thermal conductivity thk [W/m/K] of the Sturm et al. (1997) fit as implemented in SoilTemperatureMod.F90:774-778 (bw in kg/m3): thk = 0.023 + 0.234*(bw/1000) for bw <= 156, else thk = 0.138 - 1.01*(bw/1000) + 3.233*(bw/1000)^2. The traced run uses the Sturm1997 snow_thermal_cond_method. The five literals in the Fortran lack the _r8 suffix, so under default real(4) the executed coefficients are the float32-rounded values written here (0.023000000044703484, 0.23399999737739563, 0.1379999965429306, 1.0099999904632568, 3.2330000400543213) promoted to double, not the paper's coefficients (bugs.md #33; verified in the compiled object's .rodata.cst8 and against the dump to rel 1.6e-16).",
   "params": [
    "bw"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<=",
      "args": [
       "bw",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 156.0,
        "units": "kg/m^3"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.023000000044703484,
        "units": "W/m/K"
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.23399999737739563,
          "units": "W/m/K"
         },
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "bw",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1000.0,
            "units": "kg/m^3"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.1379999965429306,
        "units": "W/m/K"
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": -1.0099999904632568,
          "units": "W/m/K"
         },
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "bw",
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1000.0,
            "units": "kg/m^3"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 3.2330000400543213,
          "units": "W/m/K"
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             "bw",
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 1000.0,
              "units": "kg/m^3"
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 2,
            "units": "1"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "snow_heat_capacity": {
   "description": "Snow heat capacity cv = max(thin_sfclayer, (cpliq*h2osoi_liq + cpice*h2osoi_ice)/frac_sno_fluxes) [J/m2/K], the thin-layer floor of SoilTemperatureMod.F90:892-895 (cv is per unit ground area, h2osoi_* in kg/m2). The else branch is thin_sfclayer + 0*h2osoi_liq, value-identical to the scalar thin_sfclayer, so both branches of the ifelse under the runtime scalar condition frac_sno_fluxes > 0 share one value box, which the strict native compiler requires when the template is applied whole-array inside a const-cadence observed (esm-libraries-spec 2.5.10). The thin_sfclayer floor never binds in the dump (all snow layers have dz >= thin_sfclayer).",
   "params": [
    "h2osoi_liq",
    "h2osoi_ice",
    "frac_sno_fluxes",
    "cpliq",
    "cpice",
    "thin_sfclayer"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": ">",
      "args": [
       "frac_sno_fluxes",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "max",
      "args": [
       "thin_sfclayer",
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             "cpliq",
             "h2osoi_liq"
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             "cpice",
             "h2osoi_ice"
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         "frac_sno_fluxes"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       "thin_sfclayer",
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.0,
          "units": "J/kg/K"
         },
         "h2osoi_liq"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "stability_chik": {
   "description": "chik = sqrt(sqrt(1 - 16*zeta)), the intermediate of the Paulson (1970) momentum stability function (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:1131-1132). Factored so the 1 - 16*zeta subexpression is authored once and bound by stability_func_momentum by reference (chik2 = chik^2 of the Fortran's chik2 = sqrt(1 - 16*zeta)).",
   "params": [
    "zeta"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "sqrt",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "sqrt",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         1.0,
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           16.0,
           "zeta"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "stability_func_momentum": {
   "description": "Paulson (1970) unstable momentum stability function StabilityFunc1(zeta) of FrictionVelocityMod.F90:1131-1134: chik2 = sqrt(1 - 16*zeta), chik = sqrt(chik2), 2*log((1+chik)*0.5) + log((1+chik2)*0.5) - 2*atan(chik) + SHR_CONST_PI*0.5, with chik/chik2 bound once via the stability_chik template by reference. The trailing constant is SHR_CONST_PI*0.5 = 1.5707963267948966 exactly (clm_varcon.F90:42, rpi = SHR_CONST_PI); the cmeps psimhu_unstable hard-codes 1.571 instead, so this template is authored fresh rather than reused. Only the rib < 0 (unstable) branch is transcribed here; the stable branch of the flux-gradient relations is the linear 5*zeta form written directly in the profile templates.",
   "params": [
    "zeta"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       2.0,
       {
        "op": "log",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
             1.0,
             {
              "op": "apply_expression_template",
              "args": [],
              "name": "stability_chik",
              "bindings": {
               "zeta": "zeta"
              }
             }
            ]
           },
           0.5
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "log",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           1.0,
           {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "apply_expression_template",
              "args": [],
              "name": "stability_chik",
              "bindings": {
               "zeta": "zeta"
              }
             },
             2
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         0.5
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       -2.0,
       {
        "op": "atan",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "apply_expression_template",
          "args": [],
          "name": "stability_chik",
          "bindings": {
           "zeta": "zeta"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 1.5707963267948966,
      "units": "1"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "stability_func_scalar": {
   "description": "Paulson (1970) unstable scalar stability function StabilityFunc2(zeta) of FrictionVelocityMod.F90:1151-1152: 2*log((1 + sqrt(1 - 16*zeta))*0.5). This is exactly the cmeps psixhu_unstable (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:164) evaluated at x = (1 - 16*zeta)^0.25, so it is reused by reference (esm-spec 9.7.3) rather than re-authored.",
   "params": [
    "zeta"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "apply_expression_template",
    "args": [],
    "name": "psixhu_unstable",
    "bindings": {
     "x": {
      "op": "^",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         1.0,
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           16.0,
           "zeta"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       0.25
      ]
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "monin_obukhov_initial_wind": {
   "description": "Initial wind speed um of MoninObukIni (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:1190-1194): wc = 0.5 m/s convective velocity; if dthv >= 0 then um = max(ur, 0.1 m/s) else um = sqrt(ur^2 + wc^2). The companion initial ustar = 0.06 (F90:1189) is never read after the MoninObukIni call in BareGroundFluxesMod, so it is omitted. Also applied to the stability-iteration update of um (BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:370,373), whose branch test is zeta_raw >= 0 instead of dthv >= 0.",
   "params": [
    "dthv",
    "ur",
    "wc"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": ">=",
      "args": [
       "dthv",
       0.0
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "max",
      "args": [
       "ur",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.1,
        "units": "m/s"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "sqrt",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "ur",
           2
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "wc",
           2
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "bulk_richardson": {
   "description": "Bulk Richardson number rib of MoninObukIni (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:1196): rib = grav*zldis*dthv/(thv*um^2).",
   "params": [
    "grav",
    "zldis",
    "dthv",
    "thv",
    "um"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "grav",
       "zldis",
       "dthv"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "thv",
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "um",
         2
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "clamp_zeta": {
   "description": "Sign-preserving clamp of the Monin-Obukhov stability parameter zeta (BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:369-374 and FrictionVelocityMod.F90:1200-1204): stable/neutral branch (zeta >= 0) zeta = min(zetamaxstable, max(zeta, 0.01)), unstable branch zeta = max(-100, min(zeta, -0.01)). Shared by the MoninObukIni initialization (monin_obukhov_initial_zeta) and every pass of the BareGroundFluxes stability iteration.",
   "params": [
    "zeta",
    "zetamaxstable"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": ">=",
      "args": [
       "zeta",
       0.0
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       "zetamaxstable",
       {
        "op": "max",
        "args": [
         "zeta",
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 0.01,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "max",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": -100.0,
        "units": "1"
       },
       {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
         "zeta",
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": -0.01,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "monin_obukhov_initial_zeta": {
   "description": "Initial Monin-Obukhov stability parameter zeta of MoninObukIni (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:1198-1204). Stable/neutral branch (rib >= 0): zeta = rib*log(zldis/z0m)/(1 - 5*min(rib, 0.19)); unstable branch: zeta = rib*log(zldis/z0m); the branch result then passes through the sign-preserving clamp of clamp_zeta, shared with the stability-iteration clamp. The Obukhov length follows as obu = zldis/zeta at the call site.",
   "params": [
    "rib",
    "zldis",
    "z0m",
    "zetamaxstable"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "apply_expression_template",
    "args": [],
    "name": "clamp_zeta",
    "bindings": {
     "zeta": {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">=",
        "args": [
         "rib",
         0.0
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "rib",
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               "zldis",
               "z0m"
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           1.0,
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             5.0,
             {
              "op": "min",
              "args": [
               "rib",
               0.19
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         "rib",
         {
          "op": "log",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             "zldis",
             "z0m"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     "zetamaxstable": "zetamaxstable"
    }
   }
  },
  "stable_profile_integral": {
   "description": "The stable/neutral branches of the integrated flux-profile integral v, the denominator of the friction-velocity laws (v in ustar = vkc*um/v and temp = vkc/v), identical for the momentum (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:865-869) and scalar (F90:964-968) profiles: zeta <= 1: v = log(zldis/z0) + 5*zeta - 5*z0/obu; zeta > 1: v = log(obu/z0) + 5 - 5*z0/obu + (5*log(zeta) + zeta - 1), in the stability parameter zeta = zldis/obu. Shared by friction_velocity_momentum and friction_velocity_scalar by reference.",
   "params": [
    "zldis",
    "z0",
    "obu",
    "zeta"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "<=",
      "args": [
       "zeta",
       1.0
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "log",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "zldis",
           "z0"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         5.0,
         "zeta"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           5.0,
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             "z0",
             "obu"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "log",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           "obu",
           "z0"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       5.0,
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           5.0,
           {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
             "z0",
             "obu"
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           5.0,
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             "zeta"
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         "zeta",
         -1.0
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "friction_velocity_momentum": {
   "description": "Momentum profile: friction velocity ustar = vkc*um/v of FrictionVelocity (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:857-871), where v is the four-branch integral of the wind profile in the stability parameter zeta, passed in and computed once at the call site as zldis/obu (zetam = 1.574 is the transition point of the flux-gradient relation, F90:795). Branches: zeta < -zetam: v = log(-zetam*obu/z0m) - StabilityFunc1(-zetam) + StabilityFunc1(z0m/obu) + 1.14*((-zeta)^0.333 - zetam^0.333); zeta < 0: v = log(zldis/z0m) - StabilityFunc1(zeta) + StabilityFunc1(z0m/obu); the stable branches (zeta <= 1 and zeta > 1) are the shared stable_profile_integral, applied by reference.",
   "params": [
    "vkc",
    "um",
    "zldis",
    "z0m",
    "obu",
    "zetam",
    "zeta"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     "vkc",
     "um",
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       1.0,
       {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "<",
          "args": [
           "zeta",
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "zetam"
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                   "zetam"
                  ]
                 },
                 "obu"
                ]
               },
               "z0m"
              ]
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "apply_expression_template",
              "args": [],
              "name": "stability_func_momentum",
              "bindings": {
               "zeta": {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                 "zetam"
                ]
               }
              }
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "stability_func_momentum",
            "bindings": {
             "zeta": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               "z0m",
               "obu"
              ]
             }
            }
           },
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             1.14,
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                   "zeta"
                  ]
                 },
                 0.333
                ]
               },
               {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                 "zetam",
                 0.333
                ]
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "ifelse",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "<",
            "args": [
             "zeta",
             0.0
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "log",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                 "zldis",
                 "z0m"
                ]
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "stability_func_momentum",
                "bindings": {
                 "zeta": "zeta"
                }
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "apply_expression_template",
              "args": [],
              "name": "stability_func_momentum",
              "bindings": {
               "zeta": {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                 "z0m",
                 "obu"
                ]
               }
              }
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "stable_profile_integral",
            "bindings": {
             "zldis": "zldis",
             "z0": "z0m",
             "obu": "obu",
             "zeta": "zeta"
            }
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "friction_velocity_scalar": {
   "description": "Scalar (heat/water) profile factor temp = vkc/v of FrictionVelocity (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:956-970 for the heat profile temp1 at the measurement height; the same law with the z0q roughness and zldis = 2 + z0h/z0q serves the humidity profile temp2 (F90:974-1015, equal to temp1 when forc_hgt_q == forc_hgt_t and z0q == z0h, which holds in the traced run) and the 2-m diagnostics temp12m/temp22m (F90:1022-1038, 1051-1067)), where v is the four-branch integral of the profile in the stability parameter zeta, passed in and computed once at the call site as zldis/obu (zetat = 0.465 is the transition point of the temperature profile, F90:796). Branches: zeta < -zetat: v = log(-zetat*obu/z0) - StabilityFunc2(-zetat) + StabilityFunc2(z0/obu) + 0.8*(zetat^(-0.333) - (-zeta)^(-0.333)); zeta < 0: v = log(zldis/z0) - StabilityFunc2(zeta) + StabilityFunc2(z0/obu); the stable branches (zeta <= 1 and zeta > 1) are the shared stable_profile_integral, applied by reference.",
   "params": [
    "vkc",
    "zldis",
    "z0",
    "obu",
    "zetat",
    "zeta"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     "vkc",
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       1.0,
       {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "<",
          "args": [
           "zeta",
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             "zetat"
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                   "zetat"
                  ]
                 },
                 "obu"
                ]
               },
               "z0"
              ]
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "apply_expression_template",
              "args": [],
              "name": "stability_func_scalar",
              "bindings": {
               "zeta": {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                 "zetat"
                ]
               }
              }
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "stability_func_scalar",
            "bindings": {
             "zeta": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               "z0",
               "obu"
              ]
             }
            }
           },
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             0.8,
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                 "zetat",
                 -0.333
                ]
               },
               {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                   "zeta"
                  ]
                 },
                 -0.333
                ]
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "ifelse",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "<",
            "args": [
             "zeta",
             0.0
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "log",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                 "zldis",
                 "z0"
                ]
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "stability_func_scalar",
                "bindings": {
                 "zeta": "zeta"
                }
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "apply_expression_template",
              "args": [],
              "name": "stability_func_scalar",
              "bindings": {
               "zeta": {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                 "z0",
                 "obu"
                ]
               }
              }
             }
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "stable_profile_integral",
            "bindings": {
             "zldis": "zldis",
             "z0": "z0",
             "obu": "obu",
             "zeta": "zeta"
            }
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "z0hg_meier2022": {
   "description": "Meier2022 ground scalar-roughness update z0hg (BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:365, after Yang et al. 2008): z0hg = meier_param3*nu_param/ustar*exp(-beta_param*ustar^0.5*|tstar|^0.25), with meier_param3 = 70 (clm_varcon.F90:171), nu_param = 1.5e-5 m^2/s kinematic viscosity of air (clm_varcon.F90:165) and beta_param = 7.2 (s/m)^0.5/K^0.25 (clm_varcon.F90:164). The traced run uses z0param_method = 'Meier2022'.",
   "params": [
    "meier_param3",
    "nu_param",
    "ustar",
    "beta_param",
    "tstar"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "meier_param3",
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         "nu_param",
         "ustar"
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "exp",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           "beta_param"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "ustar",
           0.5
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "abs",
            "args": [
             "tstar"
            ]
           },
           0.25
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "z0mg_meier2022_snowmelt": {
   "description": "Meier2022 ground momentum roughness over snow-covered ground z0mg (FrictionVelocityMod.F90:620-623, the use_z0m_snowmelt = .true. branch of SetRoughnessLengthsAndForcHeightsNonLake): z0mg = exp(-b1_param*pi*0.5 + b4_param)*1e-3 when snomelt_accum < 1e-5 m, else exp(b1_param*atan((log10(snomelt_accum) + meier_param1)/meier_param2) + b4_param)*1e-3, with b1_param = 1.4, b4_param = -0.31, meier_param1 = 0.23, meier_param2 = 0.08 (clm_varcon.F90:166-170) and pi = SHR_CONST_PI = 3.141592653589793 (so pi*0.5 = 1.5707963267948966). The log10 argument is written as snomelt_accum/1 m so the unit algebra closes (the Fortran takes log10 of a length in m). The traced rows all fall in the snomelt_accum < 1e-5 branch (z0mg = exp(-1.4*pi/2 - 0.31)*1e-3 = 8.13402050576016129e-05).",
   "params": [
    "snomelt_accum",
    "b1_param",
    "b4_param",
    "meier_param1",
    "meier_param2"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.001,
      "units": "m"
     },
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "<",
        "args": [
         "snomelt_accum",
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1e-05,
          "units": "m"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "exp",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
               "b1_param"
              ]
             },
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 1.5707963267948966,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           },
           "b4_param"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "exp",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             "b1_param",
             {
              "op": "atan",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "log10",
                    "args": [
                     {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                       "snomelt_accum",
                       {
                        "op": "const",
                        "args": [],
                        "value": 1.0,
                        "units": "m"
                       }
                      ]
                     }
                    ]
                   },
                   "meier_param1"
                  ]
                 },
                 "meier_param2"
                ]
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           },
           "b4_param"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "virtual_potential_scale": {
   "description": "Virtual potential temperature scale/difference x_v = x*(1 + 0.61*forc_q) + 0.61*forc_th*y [K]: BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:328 for the difference dthv = dth*(1 + 0.61*forc_q) + 0.61*forc_th*dqh and F90:367 for the scale thvstar = tstar*(1 + 0.61*forc_q) + 0.61*forc_th*qstar. The 0.61 virtual-temperature factor is the Fortran's bare constant, transcribed with its unit.",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "forc_q",
    "forc_th",
    "y"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "x",
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 0.61,
            "units": "1"
           },
           "forc_q"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.61,
        "units": "1"
       },
       "forc_th",
       "y"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "dewpoint_magnus": {
   "description": "Dewpoint temperature [K] from vapor pressure e and temperature t (BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:548-578, dewpoint(), Equation 7 of Lawrence 2005 with the Alduchov & Eskridge 1996 coefficients): td = ifelse(t < tfrz, B1_ice*log(e/C1_ice)/(A1_ice - log(e/C1_ice)), B1_liq*log(e/C1_liq)/(A1_liq - log(e/C1_liq))) + tfrz, with A1_ice = 22.587, B1_ice = 273.86 K, C1_ice = 611.21 Pa and A1_liq = 17.625, B1_liq = 243.04 K, C1_liq = 610.94 Pa. The ice/liquid selection is on the input temperature t (t_grnd at the call site), not on the dewpoint. The traced rows all have t_grnd ~ 234-250 K < tfrz, so the ice branch is the one exercised; only the sign of t_grnd - forc_dewpoint is pinned by the raiw gate.",
   "params": [
    "e",
    "t",
    "tfrz"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "<",
        "args": [
         "t",
         "tfrz"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 273.86,
            "units": "K"
           },
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               "e",
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 611.21,
                "units": "Pa"
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 22.587,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               "e",
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 611.21,
                "units": "Pa"
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 243.04,
            "units": "K"
           },
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               "e",
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 610.94,
                "units": "Pa"
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 17.625,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "log",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
               "e",
               {
                "op": "const",
                "args": [],
                "value": 610.94,
                "units": "Pa"
               }
              ]
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     "tfrz"
    ]
   }
  },
  "sensible_heat_flux": {
   "description": "Sensible heat flux from a surface eflx_sh = -raih*(thm - t_surf) [W/m^2] (BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:449-454, applied to the ground temperature t_grnd, the top snow layer t_soisno(c, snl+1), the top soil layer t_soisno(c, 1) and the h2osfc surface).",
   "params": [
    "raih",
    "thm",
    "t_surf"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "-",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "raih",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "thm",
         "t_surf"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "evaporation_flux": {
   "description": "Evaporation flux from a surface qflx_ev = -raiw*(forc_q - qg_surf) [kg/m^2/s] (BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:460-467, applied to the ground humidity qg and the snow/soil/h2osfc surface humidities; qflx_evap_soi = -raiw*dqh with dqh = forc_q - qg of F90:327).",
   "params": [
    "raiw",
    "forc_q",
    "qg_surf"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "-",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "raiw",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "forc_q",
         "qg_surf"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "wind_stress_component": {
   "description": "One component of the surface wind stress taux/tauy = -forc_rho*forc_u/ram [kg/m/s^2] (BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:447-448, with ram = um/ustar^2 the momentum aerodynamic resistance of F90:396).",
   "params": [
    "forc_rho",
    "forc_u",
    "ram"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "-",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "forc_rho",
       "forc_u",
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         1.0,
         "ram"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "ref2m_profile": {
   "description": "2-m height profile value x_ref2m = base + temp*delta*(1/temp2m - 1/temp): the temperature and humidity profile extrapolations of BareGroundFluxesMod.F90:470 (t_ref2m = thm + temp1*dth*(1/temp12m - 1/temp1)) and F90:473 (q_ref2m = forc_q + temp2*dqh*(1/temp22m - 1/temp2)).",
   "params": [
    "base",
    "temp",
    "delta",
    "temp2m"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "base",
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "temp",
       "delta",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           1.0,
           "temp2m"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           1.0,
           "temp"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "ground_temperature_blend": {
   "description": "Area-weighted blend of the snow/soil/surface-water temperatures t = frac_sno_fluxes*t_snow + (1 - frac_sno_fluxes - frac_h2osfc)*t_soil + frac_h2osfc*t_h2osfc: the previous-time-step ground temperature t_grnd0 (SoilFluxesMod.F90:176-178) and the ground T^4 longwave-weighted temperature lw_grnd (SoilFluxesMod.F90:344-346), and the preflux ground temperature of CalcInitialTemperatureAndEnergyVars (BiogeophysPreFluxCalcsMod.F90:334-339, where the same blend appears with frac_sno_fluxes = 0 when there is no snow; the blend then reduces to (1 - frac_h2osfc)*t_soil + frac_h2osfc*t_h2osfc, the SoilFluxesMod.F90:180 no-snow branch).",
   "params": [
    "frac_sno_fluxes",
    "t_snow",
    "frac_h2osfc",
    "t_soil",
    "t_h2osfc"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "frac_sno_fluxes",
       "t_snow"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "-",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.0,
            "units": "1"
           },
           "frac_sno_fluxes"
          ]
         },
         "frac_h2osfc"
        ]
       },
       "t_soil"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "frac_h2osfc",
       "t_h2osfc"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "stefan_boltzmann_emission": {
   "description": "Black-body longwave emission law emg*sb*T4 [W/m^2]: the ground longwave emission terms of SoilFluxesMod.F90:350 (eflx_soil_grnd) and :471 (eflx_lwrad_out), with T4 the fourth power of the radiating temperature (the weighted-mean lw_grnd of SoilFluxesMod.F90:344-346) and sb the Stefan-Boltzmann constant SHR_CONST_STEBOL = 5.67e-8 (shr_const_mod.F90:23; CESM carries the rounded value rather than the CODATA 5.670374419e-8, and the stage-1 dump pins sb = 5.67e-8 exactly — see README.md).",
   "params": [
    "emg",
    "sb",
    "T4"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     "emg",
     "sb",
     "T4"
    ]
   }
  },
  "flux_temperature_correction": {
   "description": "Temperature-increment correction of a pre-solve surface flux, pre + tinc*deriv: the shift of the ground sensible/latent fluxes to the present soil temperature of SoilFluxesMod.F90:192-204 (eflx_sh_grnd = eflx_sh_grnd + tinc*cgrnds at :192, qflx_evap_soi = qflx_evap_soi + tinc*cgrndl at :193, qflx_ev_snow/qflx_ev_soil/qflx_ev_h2osfc at :202-204), with deriv the flux derivative wrt the ground temperature (cgrnds [W/m2/K] for the sensible flux, cgrndl [kg/m2/s/K] for the mass fluxes) and tinc = t_grnd - t_grnd0 the ground-temperature increment of :183. The non-urban branch is the only one transcribed (the urban branch of :197-200 replaces the soil/h2osfc partitions).",
   "params": [
    "pre",
    "tinc",
    "deriv"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "pre",
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "tinc",
       "deriv"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "stefan_boltzmann_emission_dT": {
   "description": "dT-derivative of the black-body longwave emission law, 4*emg*sb*T^3 [W/m^2/K]: d/dT(emg*sb*T^4) of the stefan_boltzmann_emission template, the linearization coefficient of the emission about the previous-time-step ground temperature. Times tinc it is the longwave increment lwrad_increment = 4*emg*sb*t_grnd0^3*tinc that SoilFluxesMod.F90:350 and :472 add into eflx_soil_grnd and eflx_lwrad_out so the ground energy balance closes when the soil temperature changes by tinc between the flux evaluation and the energy accounting (the urban eflx_lwrad_del of :361 is the same linearization at t_grnd).",
   "params": [
    "emg",
    "sb",
    "T"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 4.0,
      "units": "1"
     },
     "emg",
     "sb",
     {
      "op": "^",
      "args": [
       "T",
       3
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "psixhu_unstable": {
   "description": "Paulson (1970) unstable scalar stability function (flux_atmocn_Large.F90:164): psixhu(x) = 2*log((1 + x^2)/2), evaluated at x = xqq for the heat/water stability function psixh and at x = xqq2 for the 2-m diagnostic psix2.",
   "params": [
    "x"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "*",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 2.0,
      "units": "1"
     },
     {
      "op": "log",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": 1.0,
            "units": "1"
           },
           {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
             "x",
             {
              "op": "const",
              "args": [],
              "value": 2.0,
              "units": "1"
             }
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 2.0,
          "units": "1"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}
